{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>One lot for YHWH etc. for Azazel.</b> The Rav Avraham ben Ezra z\"l wrote: when you reach thirty-three you will know it. The explanation is: when you reach גל עד, which ascends in gematria to 33, you will find its equivalent, for that word splits into two — namely, גל עד, half by half. And here too you split this word into two: לעז אזל. And this is the sent-away goat, which goes לעז — to the cliff of the mountain, which is עז. הולך we translate אזל."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The text plays on splitting the word לעזאזל into לעז + אזל ('to the goat/scapegoat' + 'goes'), and גורל/גל עד reaching 33 by gematria; the syntax is terse and somewhat elliptical, translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:17.319663876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}